Guiding principle (how to get "exact")

To get exactly Zip2's look, you don't "restyle everything randomly".
You copy Zip2's design system and layout primitives 1:1 into ZipA, then migrate page-by-page.

That means:

Same fonts

Same Tailwind theme extensions

Same global utility classes (surface-card, btn-primary, input-field, etc.)

Same layout markup (PortalHeader + container spacing + gradient hero sections)

Phase 0 — Create a "Zip2 Design Layer" inside ZipA ✅ COMPLETE

Goal: after this phase, ZipA can render Zip2-style components without touching pages yet.

0.1 Copy Tailwind theme tokens (Zip2 → ZipA) ✅

Edit: frontend/tailwind.config.js

Add Zip2’s extensions:

fontFamily.display = var(--font-display)

fontFamily.body = var(--font-body)

color scales: slate, accent, surface

borderRadius: xl/2xl/3xl

boxShadow: surface, surface-lg

This is what makes the same class names behave the same.

0.2 Copy Zip2’s global component utility classes

Edit: frontend/src/index.css

Inside @layer components { ... } add Zip2’s classes 1:1:

.surface-card

.surface-card-hover

.surface-muted

.surface-contrast

.eyebrow

.section-title

.btn-primary

.btn-secondary

.btn-ghost

.input-field

.select-field

.pill

These classes are the “magic” that makes Zip2 look like Zip2.

0.3 Add Zip2 fonts (Space Grotesk + IBM Plex Sans)

Edit: frontend/index.html
Add <link rel="preconnect"> and Google Fonts links for:

Space Grotesk

IBM Plex Sans (400/500/600/700)

Edit: frontend/src/index.css
Add:

:root {
  --font-display: "Space Grotesk";
  --font-body: "IBM Plex Sans";
}

0.4 Make Zip2’s base body look

Zip2 uses:

font-body bg-slate-50 text-slate-900 min-h-screen

In ZipA you can apply this at the root app wrapper.

Edit: frontend/src/main.tsx
Wrap <App /> with a div:

<div className="font-body bg-slate-50 text-slate-900 min-h-screen">
  <App />
</div>


